<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000T of Jan fuel oil.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell 30,000T of Jan fuel oil.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 30,000 tonnes of 3-percent sulphur grade fuel oil for loading in January, a company offical said on Friday.</p>
<p>The cargo is to be loaded from Koahsiung between January 11-30, the official said.</p>
<p>The tender closes December 18 and is offers are valid until December 20.</p>
<p>CPC had earlier awared a term tender to sell four to six 30,000-tonne cargoes of similar grade fuel oil for loading between January and June 1997 at $3.5-$4 per tonne premia over spot quotes to a trader on free on board Koahsiung basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
